amespace>/<name>.md` owns which commands exist. The deriver fails when a command file has no `command-metadata.json` entry and no doctor route. It fails again when a declaration names a command with no file.\n108: \n109: A `command-metadata.json` entry and a doctor route or action carry the same risk keys. A value outside the accepted set fails the deriver before any policy is derived.\n110: \n111: | Risk key | Accepted values | Applies to |\n112: |---|---|---|\n113: | `mutating` | `read-only`, `add-only`, `mutates` | Every metadata entry and every doctor route or action |\n114: | `gate3_location` | A non-empty string naming what the command writes | Required on every metadata entry |\n115: | `ask_first` | `settings`, `outside-repo`, `spend`, `relaunch` | Optional on both records |\n116: | `write_scope` | `spec-folder` | Optional on both records |\n117: \n118: `derivePolicy` reads those keys in order and stops at the first match.\n119: \n120: | Step | Condition | Policy |\n121: |---|---|---|\n122: | 1 | `ask_first` lists at least one reason | `ask` |\n123: | 2 | A doctor route or action classed `mutates` | `ask` |\n124: | 3 | `mutating` is `read-only` | `run` |\n125: | 4 | `mutating` is `add-only` with `write_scope` set to `spec-folder` | `run` |\n126: | 5 | Any other record | `start` |\n127: \n128: `commandPolicies` in `command-bridges.generated.json` holds one record per command, or one record per route or action for a doctor command. Each record carries five keys: `command`, `route`, `mutating`, `askFirst`, `policy`. Nothing scores on it yet.\n129: \n130: ---\n131: \n132: ## 9. RELATED\n133: \n134: - [`Skill-advisor scripts`](../README.md)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/README.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794559694117,"end":1794559694881}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794559694888,"sessionID":"ses_e2be879acffebQYw44uGZIYT5D","part":{"partID":"prt_1d417d6c3001mFTKH1tHxucu2K","sessionID":"ses_e2be879acffebQYw44uGZIYT5D","messageID":"msg_1d417adc5001o85v322eo2oZ7S","type":"tool","id":"call_29ee60efe41e4debaee3c33f","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/README.md"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/README.md, lines 1-203\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Skill Advisor Library: Runtime, Scoring And Metadata Helpers\"\n3: description: \"TypeScript library modules for skill-advisor routing, scoring, daemon freshness, lifecycle metadata, compatibility and prompt-safe rendering.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"skill advisor library\"\n6:   - \"advisor runtime modules\"\n7:   - \"skill advisor scoring\"\n8: ---\n9: \n10: # Skill Advisor Library: Runtime, Scoring And Metadata Helpers\n11: \n12: ---\n13: \n14: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n15: \n16: `runtime/lib/` owns the TypeScript helper layer behind advisor recommendation, prompt-safe rendering, daemon freshness checks, lifecycle metadata, compatibility probes and scorer behavior. Handlers import `../lib/...` modules, and scripts call these modules instead of duplicating advisor logic.\n17: \n18: Current state:\n19: \n20: - Centralizes prompt policy, normalization, scoring and render helpers.\n21: - Groups compatibility, daemon, derived metadata, freshness, lifecycle, scorer, shadow and utility modules in focused subfolders.\n22: - Keeps subprocess and source-cache behavior close to the advisor runtime path.\n23: \n24: ---\n25: \n26: ## 2. ARCHITECTURE\n27: \n28: ```text\n29: ╭──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮\n30: │                      SKILL ADVISOR LIBRARY                       │\n31: ╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\n32: \n33: ┌──────────────┐      ┌────────────────┐      ┌──────────────────┐\n34: │ Handlers     │ ───▶ │ Runtime values │ ───▶ │ Scorer / policy  │\n35: │ scripts      │      │ render helpers │      │ normalization    │\n36: └──────┬───────┘      └───────┬────────┘      └────────┬─────────┘\n37:        │                      │                        │\n38:        │                      ▼                        ▼\n39:        │              ┌───────────────┐        ┌────────────────┐\n40:        └───────────▶  │ Freshness     │ ───▶   │ Compatibility  │\n41:                       │ daemon        │        │ lifecycle      │\n42:                       └───────┬───────┘        └────────────────┘\n43:                               │\n44:                               ▼\n45:                       ┌───────────────┐\n46:                       │ Shadow data   │\n47:                       └───────────────┘\n48: \n49: Dependency direction: handlers/scripts -> lib -> schemas and shared helpers\n50: ```\n51: \n52: ---\n53: \n54: ## 3. PACKAGE TOPOLOGY\n55: \n56: ```text\n57: lib/\n58: +-- auth/                       # Trusted caller checks\n59: +-- compat/                     # Compatibility and daemon probes\n60: +-- cross-skill-edges/          # Inbound enhances edge detection/apply helpers\n61: +-- daemon/                     # Advisor daemon helpers\n62: +-- derived/                    # Derived metadata helpers\n63: +-- embedders/                  # Advisor embedder schema and shared registry shims\n64: +-- freshness/                  # Freshness and cache state helpers\n65: +-- ipc/                        # Launcher IPC bridge and idle-timeout helpers\n66: +-- lifecycle/                  # Skill lifecycle metadata helpers\n67: +-- scorer/                     # Advisor scorer implementation\n68: +-- shadow/                     # Shadow-mode telemetry helpers\n69: +-- shared/                     # Small advisor-local shared helpers\n70: +-- utils/                      # Small utility functions\n71: +-- advisor-runtime-values.ts   # Runtime defaults and constants\n72: +-- policy-plan.ts              # Advisor policy delivery-state machine + observed-receipt confirmation (epoch>=1 floor)\n73: +-- prompt-policy.ts            # Prompt handling policy\n74: +-- render.ts                   # Prompt-safe output rendering\n75: +-- subprocess.ts               # Child-process wrapper helpers\n76: `-- README.md\n77: ```\n78: \n79: Allowed direction:\n80: \n81: ```text\n82: handlers -> lib modules\n83: scripts -> lib modules\n84: lib modules -> schemas and shared utilities\n85: ```\n86: \n87: Disallowed direction:\n88: \n89: ```text\n90: lib modules -> tool registration\n91: lib modules -> test fixtures\n92: subfolders -> handlers for runtime behavior\n93: ```\n94: \n95: ---\n96: \n97: ## 4. DIRECTORY TREE\n98: \n99: ```text\n100: lib/\n101: +-- advisor-runtime-values.ts\n102: +-- affordance-normalizer.ts\n103: +-- command-attach.ts\n104: +-- error-diagnostics.ts\n105: +-- freshness.ts\n106: +-- generation.ts\n107: +-- metrics.ts\n108: +-- normalize-adapter-output.ts\n109: +-- policy-plan.ts\n110: +-- prompt-cache.ts\n111: +-- prompt-policy.ts\n112: +-- render.ts\n113: +-- skill-advisor-brief.ts\n114: +-- source-cache.ts\n115: +-- subprocess.ts\n116: +-- cross-skill-edges/\n117: +-- embedders/\n118: +-- ipc/\n119: +-- scorer/\n120: +-- shared/\n121: `-- README.md\n122: ```\n123: \n124: ---\n125: \n126: ## 5. KEY FILES\n127: \n128: | File | Responsibility |\n129: |---|---|\n130: | `advisor-runtime-values.ts` | Runtime constants and defaults used by advisor paths. |\n131: | `affordance-normalizer.ts` | Normalizes prompt affordance signals before scoring. |\n132: | `command-attach.ts` | `attachCommand()` names the slash command for a hub recommendation whose compiled route picks one `workflowMode`. It reads the `MODE_COMMANDS` table that `derive-command-bridges.cjs` generates from each hub's `mode-registry.json`. A `system-deep-loop` command needs `/deep:` or a `DEPTH_WORDING` phrase in the prompt. The module has no imports. |\n133: | `prompt-policy.ts` | Applies prompt-safe routing and rendering policy. |\n134: | `render.ts` | Renders advisor results into prompt-safe output. |\n135: | `skill-advisor-brief.ts` | Builds concise advisor recommendation briefs. |\n136: | `normalize-adapter-output.ts` | Normalizes adapter result shapes. |\n137: | `subprocess.ts` | Wraps external process execution for advisor scripts or probes. |\n138: | `df-idf.ts` | Computes DF/IDF statistics over the active corpus, excluding archived and future skills through `lifecycle/archive-handling`, with a cached variant and a debounced updater. Only tests and the stress suite import it today. |\n139: | `route-exclusions.ts` | Loads the operator denylist of skill ids the advisor never routes: `config/route-exclusions.json`, fully replaced by a gitignored `route-exclusions.local.json` when present, or the directory in `SPECKIT_ADVISOR_ROUTE_EXCLUSIONS_DIR`. A missing or malformed file yields an empty set and never throws. |\n140: | `caller-context.ts` | Holds the per-request caller context (session id, transport, caller pid, `trusted` flag) in `AsyncLocalStorage`, read by the trusted-caller gate. |\n141: | `cross-skill-edges/` | Detects and optionally applies inbound `enhances` graph edges. |\n142: | `embedders/` | Owns advisor vector schema helpers and shared embedder shims. It names and creates both the skill vector table and the `vec_cmd_<dim>` command vector table, which has no foreign key into `skill_nodes`. |\n143: | `ipc/` | Owns launcher socket bridge and idle-timeout helpers. |\n144: | `shared/` | Keeps advisor-local shared helpers and compatibility shims. |\n145: \n146: ---\n147: \n148: ## 6. BOUNDARIES AND FLOW\n149: \n150: | Boundary | Rule |\n151: |---|---|\n152: | Imports | May import advisor schemas, shared helpers and focused local submodules. |\n153: | Exports | Export reusable advisor runtime helpers, not tool registration. |\n154: | Ownership | Keep advisor computation and metadata helpers here. Put tool handlers in `../handlers/` and CLI wrappers in `../scripts/`. |\n155: \n156: Main flow:\n157: \n158: ```text\n159: prompt or status request\n160:   -> handler or script entrypoint\n161:   -> lib policy, scorer, freshness or compatibility helper\n162:   -> prompt-safe advisor result or diagnostic payload\n163: ```\n164: \n165: ---\n166: \n167: ## 7. ENTRYPOINTS\n168: \n169: | Entrypoint | Type | Purpose |\n170: |---|---|---|\n171: | `render.ts` | Module | Formats advisor output for callers. |\n172: | `prompt-policy.ts` | Module | Applies prompt-safety and routing policy. |\n173: | `scorer/` | Folder | Native scoring implementation. |\n174: | `compat/` | Folder | Compatibility and daemon probe helpers. |\n175: | `cross-skill-edges/` | Folder | Inbound enhances edge propagation helpers. |\n176: | `embedders/` | Folder | Active embedder schema and shared registry shims. |\n177: | `freshness/` | Folder | Freshness state helpers. |\n178: | `ipc/` | Folder | Launcher IPC helpers. |\n179: | `shared/` | Folder | Shared local helper modules. |\n180: \n181: ---\n182: \n183: ## 8. VALIDATION\n184: \n185: Run from the repository root.\n186: \n187: ```bash\n188: python3 .skilled/skills/sk-doc/scripts/validate_document.py .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/README.md\n189: ```\n190: \n191: Expected result: exit code `0`.\n192: \n193: ---\n194: \n195: ## 9. RELATED\n196: \n197: - [`../README.md`](../README.md)\n198: - [`../handlers/README.md`](../handlers/README.md)\n199: - [`../scripts/README.md`](../scripts/README.md)\n200: - [`cross-skill-edges/README.md`](cross-skill-edges/README.md)\n201: - [`embedders/README.md`](embedders/README.md)\n202: - [`ipc/README.md`](ipc/README.md)\n203: - [`shared/README.md`](shared/README.md)","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/README.md, lines 1-203\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Skill Advisor Library: Runtime, Scoring And Metadata Helpers\"\n3: description: \"TypeScript library modules for skill-advisor routing, scoring, daemon freshness, lifecycle metadata, compatibility and prompt-safe rendering.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"skill advisor library\"\n6:   - \"advisor runtime modules\"\n7:   - \"skill advisor scoring\"\n8: ---\n9: \n10: # Skill Advisor Library: Runtime, Scoring And Metadata Helpers\n11: \n12: ---\n13: \n14: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n15: \n16: `runtime/lib/` owns the TypeScript helper layer behind advisor recommendation, prompt-safe rendering, daemon freshness checks, lifecycle metadata, compatibility probes and scorer behavior. Handlers import `../lib/...` modules, and scripts call these modules instead of duplicating advisor logic.\n17: \n18: Current state:\n19: \n20: - Centralizes prompt policy, normalization, scoring and render helpers.\n21: - Groups compatibility, daemon, derived metadata, freshness, lifecycle, scorer, shadow and utility modules in focused subfolders.\n22: - Keeps subprocess and source-cache behavior close to the advisor runtime path.\n23: \n24: ---\n25: \n26: ## 2. ARCHITECTURE\n27: \n28: ```text\n29: ╭──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮\n30: │                      SKILL ADVISOR LIBRARY                       │\n31: ╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\n32: \n33: ┌──────────────┐      ┌────────────────┐      ┌──────────────────┐\n34: │ Handlers     │ ───▶ │ Runtime values │ ───▶ │ Scorer / policy  │\n35: │ scripts      │      │ render helpers │      │ normalization    │\n36: └──────┬───────┘      └───────┬────────┘      └────────┬─────────┘\n37:        │                      │                        │\n38:        │                      ▼                        ▼\n39:        │              ┌───────────────┐        ┌────────────────┐\n40:        └───────────▶  │ Freshness     │ ───▶   │ Compatibility  │\n41:                       │ daemon        │        │ lifecycle      │\n42:                       └───────┬───────┘        └────────────────┘\n43:                               │\n44:                               ▼\n45:                       ┌───────────────┐\n46:                       │ Shadow data   │\n47:                       └───────────────┘\n48: \n49: Dependency direction: handlers/scripts -> lib -> schemas and shared helpers\n50: ```\n51: \n52: ---\n53: \n54: ## 3. PACKAGE TOPOLOGY\n55: \n56: ```text\n57: lib/\n58: +-- auth/                       # Trusted caller checks\n59: +-- compat/                     # Compatibility and daemon probes\n60: +-- cross-skill-edges/          # Inbound enhances edge detection/apply helpers\n61: +-- daemon/                     # Advisor daemon helpers\n62: +-- derived/                    # Derived metadata helpers\n63: +-- embedders/                  # Advisor embedder schema and shared registry shims\n64: +-- freshness/                  # Freshness and cache state helpers\n65: +-- ipc/                        # Launcher IPC bridge and idle-timeout helpers\n66: +-- lifecycle/                  # Skill lifecycle metadata helpers\n67: +-- scorer/                     # Advisor scorer implementation\n68: +-- shadow/                     # Shadow-mode telemetry helpers\n69: +-- shared/                     # Small advisor-local shared helpers\n70: +-- utils/                      # Small utility functions\n71: +-- advisor-runtime-values.ts   # Runtime defaults and constants\n72: +-- policy-plan.ts              # Advisor policy delivery-state machine + observed-receipt confirmation (epoch>=1 floor)\n73: +-- prompt-policy.ts            # Prompt handling policy\n74: +-- render.ts                   # Prompt-safe output rendering\n75: +-- subprocess.ts               # Child-process wrapper helpers\n76: `-- README.md\n77: ```\n78: \n79: Allowed direction:\n80: \n81: ```text\n82: handlers -> lib modules\n83: scripts -> lib modules\n84: lib modules -> schemas and shared utilities\n85: ```\n86: \n87: Disallowed direction:\n88: \n89: ```text\n90: lib modules -> tool registration\n91: lib modules -> test fixtures\n92: subfolders -> handlers for runtime behavior\n93: ```\n94: \n95: ---\n96: \n97: ## 4. DIRECTORY TREE\n98: \n99: ```text\n100: lib/\n101: +-- advisor-runtime-values.ts\n102: +-- affordance-normalizer.ts\n103: +-- command-attach.ts\n104: +-- error-diagnostics.ts\n105: +-- freshness.ts\n106: +-- generation.ts\n107: +-- metrics.ts\n108: +-- normalize-adapter-output.ts\n109: +-- policy-plan.ts\n110: +-- prompt-cache.ts\n111: +-- prompt-policy.ts\n112: +-- render.ts\n113: +-- skill-advisor-brief.ts\n114: +-- source-cache.ts\n115: +-- subprocess.ts\n116: +-- cross-skill-edges/\n117: +-- embedders/\n118: +-- ipc/\n119: +-- scorer/\n120: +-- shared/\n121: `-- README.md\n122: ```\n123: \n124: ---\n125: \n126: ## 5. KEY FILES\n127: \n128: | File | Responsibility |\n129: |---|---|\n130: | `advisor-runtime-values.ts` | Runtime constants and defaults used by advisor paths. |\n131: | `affordance-normalizer.ts` | Normalizes prompt affordance signals before scoring. |\n132: | `command-attach.ts` | `attachCommand()` names the slash command for a hub recommendation whose compiled route picks one `workflowMode`. It reads the `MODE_COMMANDS` table that `derive-command-bridges.cjs` generates from each hub's `mode-registry.json`. A `system-deep-loop` command needs `/deep:` or a `DEPTH_WORDING` phrase in the prompt. The module has no imports. |\n133: | `prompt-policy.ts` | Applies prompt-safe routing and rendering policy. |\n134: | `render.ts` | Renders advisor results into prompt-safe output. |\n135: | `skill-advisor-brief.ts` | Builds concise advisor recommendation briefs. |\n136: | `normalize-adapter-output.ts` | Normalizes adapter result shapes. |\n137: | `subprocess.ts` | Wraps external process execution for advisor scripts or probes. |\n138: | `df-idf.ts` | Computes DF/IDF statistics over the active corpus, excluding archived and future skills through `lifecycle/archive-handling`, with a cached variant and a debounced updater. Only tests and the stress suite import it today. |\n139: | `route-exclusions.ts` | Loads the operator denylist of skill ids the advisor never routes: `config/route-exclusions.json`, fully replaced by a gitignored `route-exclusions.local.json` when present, or the directory in `SPECKIT_ADVISOR_ROUTE_EXCLUSIONS_DIR`. A missing or malformed file yields an empty set and never throws. |\n140: | `caller-context.ts` | Holds the per-request caller context (session id, transport, caller pid, `trusted` flag) in `AsyncLocalStorage`, read by the trusted-caller gate. |\n141: | `cross-skill-edges/` | Detects and optionally applies inbound `enhances` graph edges. |\n142: | `embedders/` | Owns advisor vector schema helpers and shared embedder shims. It names and creates both the skill vector table and the `vec_cmd_<dim>` command vector table, which has no foreign key into `skill_nodes`. |\n143: | `ipc/` | Owns launcher socket bridge and idle-timeout helpers. |\n144: | `shared/` | Keeps advisor-local shared helpers and compatibility shims. |\n145: \n146: ---\n147: \n148: ## 6. BOUNDARIES AND FLOW\n149: \n150: | Boundary | Rule |\n151: |---|---|\n152: | Imports | May import advisor schemas, shared helpers and focused local submodules. |\n153: | Exports | Export reusable advisor runtime helpers, not tool registration. |\n154: | Ownership | Keep advisor computation and metadata helpers here. Put tool handlers in `../handlers/` and CLI wrappers in `../scripts/`. |\n155: \n156: Main flow:\n157: \n158: ```text\n159: prompt or status request\n160:   -> handler or script entrypoint\n161:   -> lib policy, scorer, freshness or compatibility helper\n162:   -> prompt-safe advisor result or diagnostic payload\n163: ```\n164: \n165: ---\n166: \n167: ## 7. ENTRYPOINTS\n168: \n169: | Entrypoint | Type | Purpose |\n170: |---|---|---|\n171: | `render.ts` | Module | Formats advisor output for callers. |\n172: | `prompt-policy.ts` | Module | Applies prompt-safety and routing policy. |\n173: | `scorer/` | Folder | Native scoring implementation. |\n174: | `compat/` | Folder | Compatibility and daemon probe helpers. |\n175: | `cross-skill-edges/` | Folder | Inbound enhances edge propagation helpers. |\n176: | `embedders/` | Folder | Active embedder schema and shared registry shims. |\n177: | `freshness/` | Folder | Freshness state helpers. |\n178: | `ipc/` | Folder | Launcher IPC helpers. |\n179: | `shared/` | Folder | Shared local helper modules. |\n180: \n181: ---\n182: \n183: ## 8. VALIDATION\n184: \n185: Run from the repository root.\n186: \n187: ```bash\n188: python3 .skilled/skills/sk-doc/scripts/validate_document.py .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/README.md\n189: ```\n190: \n191: Expected result: exit code `0`.\n192: \n193: ---\n194: \n195: ## 9. RELATED\n196: \n197: - [`../README.md`](../README.md)\n198: - [`../handlers/README.md`](../handlers/README.md)\n199: - [`../scripts/README.md`](../scripts/README.md)\n200: - [`cross-skill-edges/README.md`](cross-skill-edges/README.md)\n201: - [`embedders/README.md`](embedders/README.md)\n202: - [`ipc/README.md`](ipc/README.md)\n203: - [`shared/README.md`](shared/README.md)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/README.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794559694531,"end":1794559694888}}}}
