ng the entry id and every enabled runtime id. Each row carries the runnable slash command, its derived policy and the owning skill. It writes the `MODE_COMMANDS` block into the same file, one row per hub mode that names a command, and fails when a mode names a command with no file under `.skilled/commands/`. The same block also holds `TRACKED_COMMANDS`, one row per tracked command keyed by its runnable string, emitted for every bridge entry whether or not the bridge is active. A surface that attaches a command reads its policy from `TRACKED_COMMANDS`. Each TypeScript bridge in `lib/scorer/projection.ts` carries an `ownerSkill`, the skill that owns its command. The generated JSON and generated source blocks are outputs, not hand-edited inputs.\n \n Every tracked row carries the command's derived policy, the skill that owns it and `scorerRow`, which is true when the TypeScript scorer has a row for that entry. A typed command therefore always has a policy and an owner to deliver, even where no scorer row exists.\n \n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"diff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/README.md b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/README.md\nindex 7ad1c52e5d..6801401518 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/README.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/README.md\n@@ -129,7 +129,7 @@ lib/\n |---|---|\n | `advisor-runtime-values.ts` | Runtime constants and defaults used by advisor paths. |\n | `affordance-normalizer.ts` | Normalizes prompt affordance signals before scoring. |\n-| `command-attach.ts` | `attachCommand()` names the slash command for a hub recommendation whose compiled route picks one `workflowMode`. It reads the `MODE_COMMANDS` table that `derive-command-bridges.cjs` generates from each hub's `mode-registry.json`. A `system-deep-loop` command needs `/deep:` or a `DEPTH_WORDING` phrase in the prompt. The module has no imports. |\n+| `command-attach.ts` | `attachCommand()` names the slash command for a hub recommendation whose compiled route picks one `workflowMode`. It reads the `MODE_COMMANDS` table that `derive-command-bridges.cjs` generates from each hub's `mode-registry.json`. A `system-deep-loop` command needs the same command typed in the prompt or a `DEPTH_WORDING` phrase, and a prompt that matches `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` gets no command. The module has no imports. |\n | `prompt-policy.ts` | Applies prompt-safe routing and rendering policy. |\n | `render.ts` | Renders advisor results into prompt-safe output. |\n | `skill-advisor-brief.ts` | Builds concise advisor recommendation briefs. |\ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/README.md b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/README.md\nindex cfee7c4f93..1b96c78231 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/README.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/README.md\n@@ -47,7 +47,7 @@ hub mode-registry.json files\n               command-bridges.generated.json\n ```\n \n-The deriver also updates generated projection blocks in the live TypeScript and Python scoring sources. Its `GENERATED COMMAND ROWS` block in `lib/command-attach.ts` holds `COMMAND_ROWS`, one row per id a scorer can return for an enabled entry, covering the entry id and every enabled runtime id. Each row carries the runnable slash command, its derived policy and the owning skill. The same block holds `COMMAND_POLICIES`, one policy per runnable string, so a surface that attaches a command can name its policy without a second lookup. It writes the `MODE_COMMANDS` block into the same file, one row per hub mode that names a command, and fails when a mode names a command with no file under `.skilled/commands/`. The same block also holds `TRACKED_COMMANDS`, one row per tracked command keyed by its runnable string, emitted for every bridge entry whether or not the bridge is active. Each TypeScript bridge in `lib/scorer/projection.ts` carries an `ownerSkill`, the skill that owns its command. The generated JSON and generated source blocks are outputs, not hand-edited inputs.\n+The deriver also updates generated projection blocks in the live TypeScript and Python scoring sources. Its `GENERATED COMMAND ROWS` block in `lib/command-attach.ts` holds `COMMAND_ROWS`, one row per id a scorer can return for an enabled entry, covering the entry id and every enabled runtime id. Each row carries the runnable slash command, its derived policy and the owning skill. It writes the `MODE_COMMANDS` block into the same file, one row per hub mode that names a command, and fails when a mode names a command with no file under `.skilled/commands/`. The same block also holds `TRACKED_COMMANDS`, one row per tracked command keyed by its runnable string, emitted for every bridge entry whether or not the bridge is active. A surface that attaches a command reads its policy from `TRACKED_COMMANDS`. Each TypeScript bridge in `lib/scorer/projection.ts` carries an `ownerSkill`, the skill that owns its command. The generated JSON and generated source blocks are outputs, not hand-edited inputs.\n \n Every tracked row carries the command's derived policy, the skill that owns it and `scorerRow`, which is true when the TypeScript scorer has a row for that entry. A typed command therefore always has a policy and an owner to deliver, even where no scorer row exists.\n \n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff -- .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/README.md .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/README.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794559742969,"end":1794559743695}}}}
