{"type":"text","timestamp":1794559757730,"sessionID":"ses_e2be879acffebQYw44uGZIYT5D","part":{"id":"prt_1d418c183001UVU8mi4M3WXErd","sessionID":"ses_e2be879acffebQYw44uGZIYT5D","messageID":"msg_1d418aea6001PjsKivdmVenv6N","type":"text","text":"T014 done. Two README paragraphs edited, no other file touched, no checkbox ticked.\n\nFiles written:\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/README.md` — deleted the `COMMAND_POLICIES` sentence and added \"A surface that attaches a command reads its policy from `TRACKED_COMMANDS`.\"\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/README.md` — `command-attach.ts` row now reads \"A `system-deep-loop` command needs the same command typed in the prompt or a `DEPTH_WORDING` phrase, and a prompt that matches `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` gets no command\", with \"The module has no imports.\" kept.\n\nVerify, run from the repository root with `ADV=.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime`, `CBR=$ADV/scripts/command-bridges/README.md`, `LR=$ADV/lib/README.md`:\n\n```\n--- 1: COMMAND_POLICIES ---\nexit=1\n--- 2: TRACKED_COMMANDS count ---\n       2\n--- 3: NO_EDIT_REQUEST ---\n1\nexit=0\n```\n\nRead as: `rg -c \"COMMAND_POLICIES\" $CBR $LR` printed nothing (no match, exit 1), `rg -o \"TRACKED_COMMANDS\" $CBR | wc -l` printed 2 where it printed 1 before, and `rg -c \"NO_EDIT_REQUEST\" $LR` printed 1. The scoped `git diff` shows only those two hunks.\n\nNot done, because the task line does not name it: no commit, no push, no git state change, no markdown validator run.\n\nNothing is the operator's to do.","time":{"start":1794559754627,"end":1794559757730}}}
